# Test: a live edit of service { tftp-server } reaches the TFTP server.
# Initial config: tftp-server enabled with root-directory tftp-a.
# After SIGHUP:   root-directory is tftp-b, nothing else changes.
# Expected: tftpserver installs the reloaded config at apply, logs it with the
#           new root directory, and serves a file that only tftp-b holds.
#
# VALIDATES: spec-plugin-reload-applies-or-refuses row 25, AC-1: tftpserver's
#            verify/apply pair rebinds its listeners for the reloaded config
#            (tftpServer.install), and a read request is answered from the new
#            root.
# PREVENTS: the acked-and-dropped reload. With OnConfigure alone, the SDK
#           answers config-apply OK and calls nothing, so the commit succeeded
#           while the server kept serving the boot root-directory.
#
# DISCRIMINATION: client/tftp-get reads only-in-b.txt from 127.0.0.1:69 until
# the content arrives, and the test asserts its OK line. Only tftp-b holds the
# file, and only the apply handler moves the server there: with OnConfigure
# alone the server answers every read with a TFTP ERROR, the client fails,
# and the "tftp-b" expectation fails too. That an edit elsewhere under service rebinds
# nothing is proven in Go by TestConfigTxUnchangedSubtreeIsNoop
# (tftpserver/config_tx_test.go). Both roots are relative, so they resolve in
# the test's own directory, where the tmpfs blocks below write them.

# skip-os linux: a reload binds every listen-interface or fails (R-13), and an
# unprivileged Linux host cannot bind port 69, so there the reload is refused.
# Darwin ignores the interface name and binds port 69 on every address, which
# an unprivileged user may. The strict bind and the cut transfer are proven in
# Go by TestConfigTxUnbindableInterfaceFailsApply and
# TestConfigTxReloadCutsTransferInFlight (tftpserver/config_tx_test.go).

option=skip-os:value=linux
option=env:var=ze.log.tftpserver:value=info

stdin=ze-bgp:terminator=EOF_CONF
service {
	tftp-server {
		enabled true
		listen-interface lo
		root-directory tftp-a
		max-transfers 10
	}
}
EOF_CONF

tmpfs=config2.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF2
service {
	tftp-server {
		enabled true
		listen-interface lo
		root-directory tftp-b
		max-transfers 10
	}
}
EOF_CONF2

tmpfs=tftp-a/only-in-a.txt:terminator=EOF_A
content-of-tftp-a
EOF_A

tmpfs=tftp-b/only-in-b.txt:terminator=EOF_B
content-of-tftp-b
EOF_B

cmd=background:seq=1:exec=le test fixture reload/tx-protocol-sighup-trigger
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze -:stdin=ze-bgp:timeout=20s
await=stderr:contains=sighup reload complete
expect=stderr:pattern=tftpserver: config applied.*root-directory=tftp-a
expect=stderr:pattern=tftpserver: config applied.*root-directory=tftp-b
cmd=foreground:seq=3:exec=le test fixture client/tftp-get 127.0.0.1:69 only-in-b.txt content-of-tftp-b
expect=stderr:contains=OK: tftp RRQ only-in-b.txt served content-of-tftp-b
reject=stderr:contains=reload error
reject=stderr:pattern=panic
